content.text:
Found it — line 244–246:

```css
h1, h2, h3 {
  color: var(--text-primary);
}
```

`var(--text-primary)` is `#132D4C` — the dark blue. This `@layer base` rule has higher effective specificity than Tailwind utility classes for `h1`. The inline `style` on the parent div sets `color: white` but `h1` has its own rule that overrides inherited color.

The fix: add `color: inherit !important` override for h1/h2/h3 inside the hero gradient section, or simply use an inline style directly on the `<h1>`:

input.old_string:
{/* Title */}
<h1 className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
  {gameTitle}
</h1>

input.new_string:
{/* Title */}
<h1 className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: "white" }}>
  {gameTitle}
</h1>

